\title{ipodr: Option-Implied Distress Measures and Their Identified Sets}
\description{
Estimates option-implied risk-neutral distributions of a single stock and
the distress measures derived from them, and reports which of these
quantities the option quotes actually determine.
}
\details{
Workflow:
\enumerate{
\item \code{\link[=ipod_chain]{ipod_chain()}} prepares one quote date and expiry from a long data frame
of quotes (parity forward, out-of-the-money calls and puts, normalised
to \eqn{Y = S_T/F}).
\item \code{\link[=ipod_fit]{ipod_fit()}} fits the penalised maximum-entropy distribution with a
default barrier; \code{\link[=tail_prob]{tail_prob()}}, \code{\link[=rnd_summary]{rnd_summary()}} and \code{\link[=adp]{adp()}} read tail
probabilities from it; \code{\link[=ipod_profile]{ipod_profile()}} and \code{\link[=pod_select]{pod_select()}} show how the
PoD depends on the barrier.
\item \code{\link[=tail_bounds]{tail_bounds()}}, \code{\link[=call_bounds]{call_bounds()}}, \code{\link[=atm_iv_bounds]{atm_iv_bounds()}} and \code{\link[=lp_bounds]{lp_bounds()}}
give the ranges consistent with the quotes and no arbitrage.
\item \code{\link[=atm_iv]{atm_iv()}}, \code{\link[=lognormal_tail]{lognormal_tail()}}, \code{\link[=drawdown]{drawdown()}} and \code{\link[=dtd]{dtd()}} provide the
benchmarks; \code{\link[=label_events]{label_events()}}, \code{\link[=auc_test]{auc_test()}}, \code{\link[=auc_bounds]{auc_bounds()}} and
\code{\link[=first_alarm]{first_alarm()}} evaluate indicators against distress events.
}

All probabilities are risk-neutral. They are not physical default
probabilities unless calibrated.
